section: ghc-lib
synopsis: An ``ExecBreak`` now stores its ``Resume`` and ``resumeExec`` receives it explicitly
issues: #28058
mrs: !16889

description: {
- ``ExecBreak`` has a new field ``breakResume :: Resume`` with the context needed
  to resume the thread stopped at that breakpoint.
- ``resumeExec`` takes a specific ``Resume`` to continue as an extra argument,
  instead of resuming the most recent breakpoint in ``ic_resume``.
- ``resumeExec`` no longer pops the ``Resume`` off ``ic_resume``. Callers that
  rely on the ``ic_resume`` stack must now update it themselves, for instance
  if if calling ``resumeExec`` on the first ``Resume`` in the context.
}
